id: k8s.replica-set
kind: kubernetes
title: ReplicaSet
aliases: rs, replica set
tags: workloads, controllers
questions:
  - what does a ReplicaSet do?
invariant: A ReplicaSet maintains a set of identical Pods matching a selector.
answer_30s: A ReplicaSet keeps exactly N Pods matching its selector alive; a Deployment creates one ReplicaSet per template version to move traffic between versions.
answer_2m: |
  The reconciliation is: count Pods matching the selector, compare with the
  declared replicas, create or delete the difference. You almost never create
  one by hand; you read them to understand a rollout (old ReplicaSet draining,
  new ReplicaSet growing) and to roll back.
when_to_use:
  - reading rollout state; never as a top-level object in normal practice
avoid_when:
  - you want versioned rollouts (use Deployment)
commands:
  - kubectl get rs -o wide => which ReplicaSets exist and their desired/ready counts
  - kubectl describe rs/api-7d9f => why this ReplicaSet is not scaling as expected
failure_modes:
  - two ReplicaSets fighting over Pods with overlapping selectors
related:
  - k8s.deployment
  - k8s.pod
  - k8s.deployment.rolling-update
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/replicaset/
